# SSH key vectors from OpenSSH's ssh-keygen.
#
# Generated by scripts/make_ssh_vectors.py. Do not edit: every
# value here is OpenSSH's answer, and a hand edit makes it
# ours.
#
# OpenSSH_10.0p2, OpenSSL 3.0.13 30 Jan 2024
# OpenSSH_7.4p1, OpenSSL 1.0.2u  20 Dec 2019 (dsa1024, ed25519-legacy)
#
# The witness is not a dependency: nothing in the build, the
# gate or the library links it, and the tests that read this
# file need neither OpenSSH nor the network. Keys are fresh on
# every run, so every row changes when this is regenerated.
#
# `private` fields are base64 of the whole private key file,
# armour included. These keys exist only to be test vectors.
#
# Counts, asserted by the test that reads this:
#   key                      9
#   encrypted                83
#   sshsig                   14

